{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>lest, as in the day of her birth</b> — when she was in Egypt, as Ezekiel mentioned: \"and you were naked and bare.\"" "<b>and I will set her</b> — like \"and he set [ויצג] the sticks.\"" "<b>and I will make her like a wilderness</b> — with no person in it." "<b>and the meaning of \"with thirst\"</b> — because she says: \"my bread-givers, my water-givers, and my drink.\""], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase ואת עירום ועריה corresponds to Ezekiel 16:7, not 16:4 which also uses the language of the day of birth; Ibn Ezra's citation may be approximate."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:47.990642450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}